The '''Grand Temple's throne room''' was a ceremonial hall located within the [[Great Temple]], on [[Yavin 4]]. On the morning after the [[Battle of Yavin]], the throne room housed the [[Royal Award Ceremony]], during which heroes of the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] were saluted.

==History==
[[File:Medal-ceremony-Yavin-4.png|thumb|left|250px|The Royal Award Ceremony that followed the Battle of Yavin]]
The [[throne]] room was a part of the [[Great Temple]], an edifice constructed by the [[Massassi]] people on the [[Yavin 4|fourth]] [[moon]] of [[Yavin Prime|Yavin]]<ref name="PSFB" /> over 5,000 [[Standard year|years]] before the [[Battle of Yavin]].<ref name="Journey Through Space (2015)" />

Long after the temple was left derelict by its original builders, it was rehabilitated by the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]], a freedom-fighting movement that liked to use preexisting structures on remote [[planet]]s to better hide its activities against the [[Galactic Empire]].<ref name="PSFB" /> After the Alliance led a successful [[Battle of Yavin|assault]] on the Empire's [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]] [[battle station]], the heroes of that victory were saluted in a [[Royal Award Ceremony]] that took place in the Temple's throne room.<ref name="ANH" />

==Layout==
The throne room was a vast chamber whose long sloped floor was paved with rectangular slabs<ref name="ANH" /> of translucent precious [[stone]].<ref name="CL 2016">[[Star Wars: Complete Locations (2016)|''Star Wars: Complete Locations'']]</ref> Its towering stone walls and high ceilings were carved with intricate patterns.<ref name="PSFB" /> The roof of the chamber was pierced by tall skylights aligned with solstice and equinox.<ref name="CL 2016" /> At the back of the room, across from the entrance, there was a ceremonial podium reached by a flight of stairs. The back wall also boasted five large window-slits that insured an abundant supply of natural light.<ref name="ANH" /> When the [[jungle]] outside was in full bloom, the air within the chamber became filled with floral scents.<ref name="PSFB" /> Behind the podium, a small hidden stairway led to an observation platform at the temple's apex.<ref name="CL 2016" />

